@section rest_history History

@subsection rest_history_get GET /api/history?is_admin={true|false}&from={date}&to={date}&show_all={true|false}&limit={n}&offset={n}&action={type}

Returns a JSON array of history rows.  Optional query parameters:
- `is_admin=true` — include admin-only actions
- `from=<ISO-date>` — filter from date (inclusive)
- `to=<ISO-date>` — filter to date (inclusive)
- `show_all=true` — show all records regardless of user
- `limit=N` — maximum number of rows to return (0 = unlimited)
- `offset=N` — skip the first N matching rows (pagination)
- `action=<type>` — only rows of this action type (`acquisition`,
  `liquidation`, `lending`, `return`, `reservation`); empty or missing =
  all types (since 2.3)

Row schema:

| Field          | Type   | Description                            |
|----------------|--------|----------------------------------------|
| `id`           | int    | Record ID                              |
| `datetime`     | string | ISO 8601 timestamp                     |
| `action`       | string | Action type (`lend`, `return`, etc.)   |
| `item_name`    | string | Item name                              |
| `count`        | int    | Count                                  |
| `user_name`    | string | Logged-in user name                    |
| `collector`    | string | Data collector name                    |
| `item_id`      | int    | Item ID                                |
| `person_id`    | int    | Person ID                              |
| `remarks`      | string | Remarks                                |
| `collector_id` | int    | Collector ID                           |
| `duedate`      | string | Due date (lendings only)               |

@subsection rest_history_conflicts GET /api/history/conflicts

Returns a JSON array of history rows that have unresolved conflicts.

@subsection rest_history_change_conflicts GET /api/history/change-conflicts

Returns a JSON array of recently changed history rows with conflicts.

@subsection rest_history_put PUT /api/history/{id}

Overwrites a history record (admin undo/redo).  Request body: history
row JSON.

@subsection rest_history_delete DELETE /api/history

Deletes all history records.

---

@section rest_classes Class Management

@subsection rest_classes_list GET /api/classes

Returns a JSON array of class name strings.

@subsection rest_classes_post POST /api/classes

Creates a new class.  Request body: `{"name":"..."}`.

@subsection rest_classes_put PUT /api/classes/{name}

Renames a class.  Request body: `{"name":"..."}` (new name).

@subsection rest_classes_delete DELETE /api/classes/{name}

Deletes a class.

@subsection rest_classes_affected GET /api/classes/affected-persons

Returns a JSON array of `AffectedPerson` objects for persons whose
class is about to change:

| Field         | Type   | Description         |
|---------------|--------|---------------------|
| `person_id`   | int    | Person ID           |
| `display_name`| string | Display name        |
| `old_class`   | string | Current class       |
| `new_class`   | string | Proposed new class  |

@subsection rest_classes_yearchanges POST /api/classes/year-changes

Applies the pending year-level class changes.

---

@section rest_reservations Reservations

Requires permission `reserve` for all endpoints.

@subsection rest_reservations_list GET /api/reservations

Returns active reservations.  Optional query parameters:
- `person_id=N` — filter by person
- `item_id=N` — filter by item (same as `/api/items/{id}/reservations`)

**Ownership rule:** callers without `edit_reservations` always receive only
their own reservations, regardless of the `person_id` query parameter.
Callers with `edit_reservations` receive all reservations (or the filtered
subset if `person_id` is given).

@subsection rest_item_reservations GET /api/items/{id}/reservations

Returns all active (non-expired) reservations for item `{id}`.

@subsection rest_reservations_post POST /api/reservations

Creates a reservation.  Request body: `Reservation` JSON (required:
`item_id`, `person_id`, `count`, `expires_at`).  Response: `{"id":N}`.

Since 1.12, if the person already has an active reservation for the
item, its count is increased by `count` instead (the existing expiry
date is kept) and the response carries the id of that reservation;
earlier versions returned HTTP 409 in this case.

- HTTP 422 if not enough unreserved copies remain.
- HTTP 403 if reservations are disabled for the item or collection.

**Ownership rule:** callers without `edit_reservations` (and without
`collect_lendings`) have `person_id` forced to their own person ID,
regardless of what is supplied in the request body.

@subsection rest_reservations_delete DELETE /api/reservations/{id}

Deletes the reservation.  Callers with `edit_reservations` may delete
any reservation; other users may only delete their own reservation and
receive HTTP 403 if they attempt to delete another person's reservation.

---

@section rest_undo Undo / Redo

The server supports undo and redo for all six entity types.

@subsection rest_undo_get GET /api/{entity}/{id}

Used during undo to retrieve the previous state of a record.

@subsection rest_undo_put PUT /api/{entity}/{id}

Used during undo/redo to write back a previous or next state.

Where `{entity}` is one of `items`, `persons`, `lendings`, `returns`,
`acquisitions`, `liquidations`.

---

@section rest_item_json Item JSON Schema

| Field               | Type    | Description                          |
|---------------------|---------|--------------------------------------|
| `id`                | int     | Item ID (0 for new)                  |
| `type_id`           | int     | Item type ID (required)              |
| `name`              | string  | Item name                            |
| `barcode`           | string  | Barcode string                       |
| `isbn`              | string  | ISBN                                 |
| `ean`               | string  | EAN                                  |
| `remarks`           | string  | Remarks                              |
| `collector`         | string  | Data-collector name                  |
| `keywords`          | array   | Array of keyword strings             |
| `values`            | object  | Map of attribute key → string value  |
| `list_values`       | object  | Map of attribute key → string list   |
| `academic_year`     | string  | Academic year string                 |
| `version`           | int     | Optimistic-concurrency version       |

---

@section rest_person_json Person JSON Schema

| Field          | Type   | Description                        |
|----------------|--------|------------------------------------|
| `id`           | int    | Person ID (0 for new)              |
| `lastname`     | string | Last name                          |
| `firstname`    | string | First name                         |
| `title`        | string | Title / class                      |
| `barcode`      | string | Person barcode                     |
| `external_id`  | string | External identifier                |
| `remarks`      | string | Remarks                            |
| `collector`    | string | Data-collector name                |
| `has_password` | bool   | Whether a password is set          |
| `version`      | int    | Optimistic-concurrency version     |

---

@section rest_lending_json Lending JSON Schema

| Field       | Type   | Required | Description                     |
|-------------|--------|----------|---------------------------------|
| `id`        | int    | no       | Lending ID (0 for new)          |
| `item_id`   | int    | yes      | Item ID                         |
| `person_id` | int    | yes      | Borrower person ID              |
| `count`     | int    | yes      | Number lent                     |
| `datetime`  | string | no       | ISO 8601 lending timestamp      |
| `duedate`   | string | no       | ISO 8601 due date               |
| `remarks`   | string | no       | Remarks                         |
| `collector` | string | no       | Data-collector name             |
| `version`   | int    | no       | Optimistic-concurrency version  |

---

@section rest_return_json Return JSON Schema

| Field        | Type   | Required | Description                    |
|--------------|--------|----------|--------------------------------|
| `id`         | int    | no       | Return ID (0 for new)          |
| `lending_id` | int    | yes      | Associated lending ID          |
| `count`      | int    | yes      | Number returned                |
| `datetime`   | string | no       | ISO 8601 return timestamp      |
| `remarks`    | string | no       | Remarks                        |
| `collector`  | string | no       | Data-collector name            |
| `version`    | int    | no       | Optimistic-concurrency version |

---

@section rest_acquisition_json Acquisition JSON Schema

| Field       | Type   | Required | Description                    |
|-------------|--------|----------|--------------------------------|
| `id`        | int    | no       | Acquisition ID (0 for new)     |
| `item_id`   | int    | yes      | Item ID                        |
| `count`     | int    | yes      | Number acquired                |
| `datetime`  | string | no       | ISO 8601 timestamp             |
| `remarks`   | string | no       | Remarks                        |
| `collector` | string | no       | Data-collector name            |
| `version`   | int    | no       | Optimistic-concurrency version |

---

@section rest_liquidation_json Liquidation JSON Schema

| Field       | Type   | Required | Description                    |
|-------------|--------|----------|--------------------------------|
| `id`        | int    | no       | Liquidation ID (0 for new)     |
| `item_id`   | int    | yes      | Item ID                        |
| `count`     | int    | yes      | Number liquidated              |
